 "source": "hardware/demo/kicad/aqroot-demo/*.kicad_sch instance properties, at D-750",
 "why": "FAB12b.  The references whose PACKAGE IDENTITY is load-bearing: every connector, every converter, every radio, the charger, the fuel gauge, the microphone, the protection FETs and the crystal.  Pinned here so a later regeneration cannot silently change one, which is the defect D-750 found on J5: D-237 moved the footprint and the datasheet URL to the 1x24 SSQ-124-02-G-S-RA and left the MPN, the LCSC code and the description on the superseded 2x12 BCS-112-S-D-HE, and every release BOM carried the wrong purchasing identity for eight months of decisions.  A pin is a REGRESSION instrument and cannot find an identity that was already wrong when it was written -- FAB12a, which reads the row's own words against the footprint's own pads, is the one that finds those. D-765: U22 was pinned and U20 -- THE OTHER HALF OF THE SAME ONE-MPN ACCESSORY PAIR -- was not, so a divergence between the two accessory limiters could not be seen here at all.  Both are pinned now, on the TPS22950-Q1 that replaced the TPS22950C.  D-766 REPINNED Q11 AO3400A -> AO3422 and NOTHING ELSE: the backlight true-off disconnect's drain reaches the 39 V this board's own .kicad_dru publishes for LED_BOOST under TPS61169 open-LED protection, and the AO3400A is a 30 V part.  SAME SOT-23 footprint, SAME 1=G/2=S/3=D pinout, so the Footprint field is unchanged -- which is exactly why this pin has to carry Value and MPN as well.  Q1, the IR driver, KEEPS the AO3400A: its drain never leaves the 5 V domain."
}
